Short:        MPEG-1 video decoder library (pl_mpeg)
Author:       Brian King; pl_mpeg by Dominic Szablewski
Uploader:     Brian King
Type:         util/libs
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     68020+
Replaces:     -

mpegv.library decodes MPEG-1 video by the CPU, for any program, as
mpega.library decodes MPEG audio. A 68020 or better; no FPU needed.

- Program Streams (.mpg, a VCD's .dat) are demultiplexed as they are
  read: the video decoded, the other packets (MPEG audio, private stream
  1) handed to the program with their times, for mpega.library or
  ac3.library. Bare video streams (.m1v) too.
- Pictures in display order as the decoder's own Y, Cb and Cr planes,
  not copied, with integer 90 kHz times.
- B pictures can be passed over when the CPU is behind.
- Helpers: packed YUV 4:2:2 for a graphics card's overlay (Picasso96's
  PIP, which scales it), RGB in eight formats for WritePixelArray, 8-bit
  greys for an AGA screen (WriteChunkyPixels).

The decoder is pl_mpeg by Dominic Szablewski, made about 2.6 times faster
on a 68020, its pictures the same bit for bit. A VCD picture (352 x 240)
takes about 11.5 million 68020 cycles; an emulated 68060 decodes one in
about 4 ms.

Contents:

  mpegv/Libs/mpegv.library      copy to LIBS:
  mpegv/Include/                libraries, clib, inline and proto headers
  mpegv/mpegv.doc               the autodoc
  mpegv/mpegv_lib.sfd
  mpegv/Example/mpvplay         plays a file's pictures (RTG: in a window,
                                RGB; AGA: a screen of greys); and its source
  mpegv/Source/                 everything, with the tests

Licence: MIT (mpegv/LICENSE), the library and pl_mpeg alike.

Source: https://github.com/luvwagn/mpegv.library

History:
1.0  First release. Made for AmigaMCE.
